  settings: {"output_format":"json","save_output":true,"output_filename":"process-proofs/printed-replacement-part/mixed-default-071/outputs/{{wright.run_id}}/source-model-report.json","file_policy":"overwrite","run_path_template":"wright.run-path/1","authoring_template":"mcp-task","mcp_server":"proof-083-blender-prompt-055","max_tool_calls":2,"timeout_seconds":360,"expected_files":"process-proofs/printed-replacement-part/mixed-default-071/outputs/{{wright.run_id}}/source_mesh.stl","task_guidance":"Use only actual selected tools; retain raw failures and observations. Never fabricate files, measurements, reviews or provider approval.","expected_file_ports":{"source_mesh":"process-proofs/printed-replacement-part/mixed-default-071/outputs/{{wright.run_id}}/source_mesh.stl"}}
  tool: null
  reusable_step: null
  prompt: "Use the existing Blender execute_blender_code tool to construct the reviewed focus wheel from the actual supplied image and dimensions. Wright runs this stage only after consuming its declared exact-subject basis review. The reviewed_basis input remains the unchanged proposed design; use the design released by that order barrier rather than treating its earlier proposal status as a new runtime question. A labelled integration-test decision permits digital construction only and is not human engineering acceptance; retain final measured-feature/support/package review. Work only with uniquely named owned objects and actual geometry. Export binary STL in explicit millimetres at 'C:\\\\Users\\\\markb\\\\.codex\\\\visualizations\\\\2026\\\\09\\\\24\\\\01a0d4b8-b5fa-79d0-8e8b-fc78c3dfd056\\\\t047-fresh-prompt-055\\\\process-proofs\\\\printed-replacement-part\\\\mixed-default-071\\\\outputs\\\\{{wright.run_id}}\\\\source_mesh.stl'. Preserve the complete original feature requirements; do not substitute a cylinder/cube or infer verified fit. Keep <=80000 triangles. Return compact actual construction observations and unresolved physical limits; Wright retains the exact tool call. Do not request an undeclared review or missing construction choice. If the released design cannot be implemented within original limits, return an explicit blocked technical outcome instead of making up evidence. Use guarded bpy/bmesh/mathutils modelling and Blender STL export only: no open/pathlib/os/sys/hashlib/runpy/subprocess/network/handlers/timers/drivers/addon operations or raw filesystem calls. Do not overwrite unrelated objects. Geometry failure is explicit; no fabricated export or verdict. The connected original_user_prompt is the user's supplied text, distinct from these task instructions and reviewed_basis. Preserve that original text verbatim in user_prompt for each execute_blender_code call; do not replace it with a task summary. Interpret the actual connected original_reference image with the supplied 38 mm scale and written dimensions governing. The connected original_context and original_user_profile retain manufacturing and use constraints. A configured recipe does not replace those inputs or establish measured compliance. Use the code argument in qualified_operation as the supplied native construction recipe. Submit it unchanged to execute_blender_code; do not invent another modelling algorithm or replace its dimensions. Its export path and owned names are configured for this fresh run. Keep actual tool observations and failures. This is reuse of a prior qualified operation, not new AI-authored geometry code or proof of compliance. If its input design differs from reviewed_basis, stop with a technical mismatch before executing it."
end

